1️⃣ Install Thunder Client Extension

Open VS Code.

Go to the Extensions tab (sidebar or Ctrl+Shift+X / Cmd+Shift+X).

Search for Thunder Client.

Click Install.

2️⃣ Open Thunder Client

After installing, you’ll see a Thunder Client icon on the left sidebar.

Click it to open the interface.

3️⃣ Create a New Request

Click New Request.

Select HTTP Method:

POST for adding data

GET for fetching data

Enter the URL:

http://localhost:3000/users/add   (for POST)
http://localhost:3000/users/list  (for GET)

4️⃣ Add JSON Body (for POST)

Click the Body tab → select JSON.

Enter your JSON data:

{
  "name": "Subasri"
}

5️⃣ Send the Request

Click Send.

You will see the response in Thunder Client, e.g.:

{
  "success": true,
  "message": "User Subasri registered successfully."
}


For GET /users/list:

[
  { "name": "Subasri
  }
]